summary:
  The devices the widget says it casts to are counted from the ticks, so
  one that refused the stream is among them.

history:
  A device that refuses stays ticked, which is as decided: the next station
  is offered to it again. With a television playing and a Ruark that had
  refused beside it, the footer, the button's hint and the panel's hint
  all read "Casting to 2 devices" (2026-11-12). The name is made from the
  record of who plays or is still being asked.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
      readonly property string _castName: { var on = CastLogic.carriers(_castSession, _castTargets);

replace:
      readonly property string _castName: { var on = _castTargets;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_failed_cast_says_which_kind_it_was_and_names_only_who_carries_the_stream.
  Line-neutral.
